From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: musa <musa@local>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:02:09 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] MUSA: let the DeepSeek-V4 router read the BF16 gate output

On MUSA the gate GEMM runs in BF16 and GateLinear cast its output to
FP32 in a separate kernel before routing. The MUSA biased router widens
BF16 logits itself, which is exact, so the non-hash DeepSeek-V4 MoE
layers keep the gate output in BF16.
---
 vllm/models/deepseek_v4/nvidia/model.py | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/vllm/models/deepseek_v4/nvidia/model.py b/vllm/models/deepseek_v4/nvidia/model.py
index d874c96daa..57166bfbbb 100644
--- a/vllm/models/deepseek_v4/nvidia/model.py
+++ b/vllm/models/deepseek_v4/nvidia/model.py
@@ -890,6 +890,16 @@ class DeepseekV4MoE(nn.Module):
                 requires_grad=False,
             )
 
+        if (
+            current_platform.is_musa()
+            and not self.use_mega_moe
+            and self.gate.tid2eid is None
+            and self.gate.e_score_correction_bias is not None
+        ):
+            # MUSA: the biased router widens the BF16 gate output itself, which
+            # saves an FP32 cast kernel per layer.
+            self.gate.out_dtype = None
+
         if config.n_shared_experts is None:
             self.shared_experts = None
         else:
-- 
